","lesson":"en-b1-14","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-15','en-b1-15',null,3,15,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-15","baseId":"en-b1-15","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":15,"title":"-ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such","objective":"His qiluvchi odamni sabab bo‘luvchi narsadan ajratasiz.","context":"Ikki o‘quvchi film ko‘rgandan keyin fikr bildiradi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-14"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi.","So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang.","Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin."],"pattern":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","examples":["The film was interesting.","I was interested in the story.","The long introduction was boring.","We were bored at first.","It was such a useful discussion.","The ending was so surprising."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-15-v0","term":"interested","meaning":"qiziqqan","ipa":"/ˈɪntrəstɪd/","collocation":"interested in","example":"I was interested in the story."},{"id":"en-b1-15-v1","term":"surprising","meaning":"hayrat uyg‘otadigan","ipa":"/səˈpraɪzɪŋ/","collocation":"a surprising ending","example":"The ending was so surprising."},{"id":"en-b1-15-v2","term":"discussion","meaning":"muhokama","ipa":"/dɪˈskʌʃən/","collocation":"a useful discussion","example":"It was such a useful discussion."},{"id":"en-b1-15-v3","term":"ending","meaning":"yakun","ipa":"/ˈendɪŋ/","collocation":"the film’s ending","example":"The ending was so surprising."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"compare","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","The film was interesting.","I was interested in the story."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Ikki o‘quvchi film ko‘rgandan keyin fikr bildiradi.","The long introduction was boring.","It was such a useful discussion."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"We were bored at first.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-15-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-15-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ot birikmasi bilan to‘g‘ri shakl?","answers":["such an interesting film"],"explanation":"Such + an + sifat + ot.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["such an interesting film","so an interesting film","such interesting an film"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I am interested ___ science.","answers":["in"],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["The film was interesting."],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","tokens":["The","film","was","interesting."]},{"id":"en-b1-15-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I was boring because the introduction was long. (his)","answers":["I was bored because the introduction was long."],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["qiziqqan","hayrat uyg‘otadigan","muhokama","yakun"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","left":["interested","surprising","discussion","ending"],"options":["qiziqqan","hayrat uyg‘otadigan","muhokama","yakun"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["interested","surprising","discussion","ending"],"options":["interested in","a surprising ending","a useful discussion","the film’s ending"],"answers":["interested in","a surprising ending","a useful discussion","the film’s ending"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."}],"reading":{"title":"-ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such — vaziyat","text":"Our club watched a short film about a young inventor. The introduction was slow, so some students were bored at first. Once the main problem appeared, the story became interesting. I was interested in how the character tested different ideas rather than simply finding a perfect answer. The ending was surprising because his first plan failed, but a smaller change solved the problem. After the film, we had such a useful discussion that I wrote a page of notes. One student said the film was too difficult, while another said the pictures helped her understand it. We agreed that a review should explain these opinions, not only use words like good or bad. The film was entertaining, but the discussion helped us connect it to our own project mistakes.","sentences":["Our club watched a short film about a young inventor.","The introduction was slow, so some students were bored at first.","Once the main problem appeared, the story became interesting.","I was interested in how the character tested different ideas rather than simply finding a perfect answer.","The ending was surprising because his first plan failed, but a smaller change solved the problem.","After the film, we had such a useful discussion that I wrote a page of notes.","One student said the film was too difficult, while another said the pictures helped her understand it.","We agreed that a review should explain these opinions, not only use words like good or bad.","The film was entertaining, but the discussion helped us connect it to our own project mistakes."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-15-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega so‘zlovchi qiziqdi?","answers":["the character tested ideas"],"explanation":"Qiziqish sababini aniq tushuntiradi.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["the character tested ideas","the introduction was long","the film had no problem"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Foydali review nima qiladi?","answers":["explains opinions with reasons"],"explanation":"Matn reason talab qiladi.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["explains opinions with reasons","only says good","lists all words"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["Our club watched a short film about a young inventor.","The introduction was slow, so some students were bored at first.","Once the main problem appeared, the story became interesting.","I was interested in how the character tested different ideas rather than simply finding a perfect answer.","The ending was surprising because his first plan failed, but a smaller change solved the problem.","After the film, we had such a useful discussion that I wrote a page of notes.","One student said the film was too difficult, while another said the pictures helped her understand it.","We agreed that a review should explain these opinions, not only use words like good or bad.","The film was entertaining, but the discussion helped us connect it to our own project mistakes."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"The introduction was boring, and we were bored. Then the story became interesting. I was interested in the inventor’s tests. The ending was so surprising, and we had such a useful discussion afterward.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-15.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-15-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Boshida odamlar holati?","answers":["bored"],"explanation":"People were bored.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["bored","boring","interested throughout"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Yakun qanday?","answers":["surprising"],"explanation":"So surprising.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["surprising","unchanged","known from the start"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["boring","bored"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","rows":["Kirish sifati","Odamlar hissi"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["We were bored at first."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-15-dictation.mp3","transcript":"We were bored at first."}]},"writing":{"task":"Film yoki kitob review yozing; his, sabab va bitta asoslangan tavsiya qo‘shing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I watched a short film about a student inventor. The introduction was rather boring, and I was bored during the first few minutes. However, the main story was interesting because it showed several failed experiments. I was interested in the way the character used feedback. The ending was so surprising that our group discussed it for half an hour. It was such a useful conversation because we could compare the mistakes with our own work. I recommend the film to students who enjoy practical projects. The language may be difficult in places, but the pictures make the main ideas clear.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["The film was interesting.","I was interested in the story.","The long introduction was boring."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bir asarni taqqoslab, nimani his qilganingiz va nima sabab bo‘lganini tushuntiring.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Film yoki kitob review yozing; his, sabab va bitta asoslangan tavsiya qo‘shing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-15-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The film was ___. (qiziqarli)","answers":["interesting"],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I was ___. (qiziqdim)","answers":["interested"],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"such ___ useful discussion","answers":["a"],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"So bilan mos qolip?","answers":["so surprising"],"explanation":"So + sifat.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["so surprising","so a surprising ending","such surprising without noun"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Hisni bildiradigan sifat qaysi?","answers":["bored"],"explanation":"Bored his qiluvchi holat.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["bored","boring","entertaining"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-15-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["I was interested in the story."],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","tokens":["I","was","interested","in","the","story."]},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I was ___. (qiziqdim)","answers":["interested"],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film"},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["We were bored at first."],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","tokens":["We","were","bored","at","first."]},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"So bilan mos qolip?","answers":["so surprising"],"explanation":"So + sifat.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["so surprising","so a surprising ending","such surprising without noun"]},{"id":"en-b1-15-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The ending was so surprising."],"explanation":"Interested odamning his holati; interesting qiziqish uyg‘otuvchi narsaning belgisi. Bored va boring ham shu farqni ko‘rsatadi. So + sifat/ravish: so interesting. Such + ot birikmasi: such an interesting film. A/an joylashuvini saqlang. Too qanchaliklikdan tashqari muammo yoki ortiqlikni bildiradi. So interesting ijobiy, too difficult vazifaga ortiqcha qiyinlik bo‘lishi mumkin.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","tokens":["The","ending","was","so","surprising."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-15","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-16','en-b1-16',null,3,16,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-16","baseId":"en-b1-16","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":16,"title":"Although, however, while: sabab va farq","objective":"Bir-biriga zid yoki sababli fikrlarni ravon bog‘laysiz.","context":"Telefon bilan o‘qishning foydasi va chalg‘itishi baholanadi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-15"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas.","However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang.","While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang."],"pattern":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","examples":["Although the task was difficult, I continued.","The app is useful. However, it can distract me.","Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading.","I took notes because the talk was long.","The room was noisy, so we moved.","I practised until the instructions were clear."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-16-v0","term":"distract","meaning":"chalg‘itmoq","ipa":"/dɪˈstrækt/","collocation":"distract attention","example":"The app is useful. However, it can distract me."},{"id":"en-b1-16-v1","term":"prefer","meaning":"afzal ko‘rmoq","ipa":"/prɪˈfɜː/","collocation":"prefer reading","example":"Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading."},{"id":"en-b1-16-v2","term":"continue","meaning":"davom ettirmoq","ipa":"/kənˈtɪnjuː/","collocation":"continue working","example":"Although the task was difficult, I continued."},{"id":"en-b1-16-v3","term":"attention","meaning":"diqqat","ipa":"/əˈtenʃən/","collocation":"pay attention","example":"pay attention"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","Although the task was difficult, I continued.","The app is useful. However, it can distract me."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Telefon bilan o‘qishning foydasi va chalg‘itishi baholanadi.","Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading.","The room was noisy, so we moved."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"I took notes because the talk was long.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-16-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-16-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Farqni ravon bog‘lang.","answers":["Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading."],"explanation":"While bu yerda taqqoslash.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading.","Lola likes audio because Ali prefers reading (cause).","Lola likes audio so while."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The room was noisy, ___ we moved.","answers":["so"],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Although the task was difficult, I continued."],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","tokens":["Although","the","task","was","difficult,","I","continued."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Although it was difficult, but I continued.","answers":["Although it was difficult, I continued."],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["chalg‘itmoq","afzal ko‘rmoq","davom ettirmoq","diqqat"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","left":["distract","prefer","continue","attention"],"options":["chalg‘itmoq","afzal ko‘rmoq","davom ettirmoq","diqqat"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-dialogue","type":"dialogue","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Sherik: “Can you give one example?” Siz: darsdagi birinchi namunani qayta tuzing.","answers":["Although the task was difficult, I continued."],"tokens":["Although","the","task","was","difficult,","I","continued."],"hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas."},{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Subject va object questions: Qabul qiluvchini so‘raydigan savol?","answers":["Who did you send it to?"],"explanation":"Who obyekt, you ega.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Who did you send it to?","Who sent it?","What happened?"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Subject va object questions"},{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Question tags va tasdiqlash ohangi: Inkor gap tagini tanlang: He didn’t call, …","answers":["did he?"],"explanation":"Inkor gap → tasdiq did he.","hint":"You’re ready, aren’t you? / She likes it, doesn’t she?","options":["did he?","didn’t he?","does he?"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Question tags va tasdiqlash ohangi"},{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · -ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such: Ot birikmasi bilan to‘g‘ri shakl?","answers":["such an interesting film"],"explanation":"Such + an + sifat + ot.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["such an interesting film","so an interesting film","such interesting an film"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"-ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such"}],"reading":{"title":"Although, however, while: sabab va farq — vaziyat","text":"Using a phone for English practice can be convenient because audio and dictionaries are easy to reach. However, the same device can distract us with messages. Lola prefers listening to short recordings, while Ali likes reading on paper. Neither method is best for every task. Although a learning app helps me practise vocabulary, I still need to use new phrases in conversation. Last week our study room was noisy, so we moved to the library. We switched off unrelated notifications and agreed on a clear aim for twenty minutes. The session went better because we knew what to finish. This does not mean phones are always bad or paper is always better. A useful choice depends on the task, the learner and the way the tool is used. We now discuss the purpose before choosing the device.","sentences":["Using a phone for English practice can be convenient because audio and dictionaries are easy to reach.","However, the same device can distract us with messages.","Lola prefers listening to short recordings, while Ali likes reading on paper.","Neither method is best for every task.","Although a learning app helps me practise vocabulary, I still need to use new phrases in conversation.","Last week our study room was noisy, so we moved to the library.","We switched off unrelated notifications and agreed on a clear aim for twenty minutes.","The session went better because we knew what to finish.","This does not mean phones are always bad or paper is always better.","A useful choice depends on the task, the learner and the way the tool is used.","We now discuss the purpose before choosing the device."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-16-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Muallifning asosiy fikri?","answers":["choose tools according to purpose"],"explanation":"Oxirgi gap purpose-first tanlovni aytadi.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["choose tools according to purpose","phones are always bad","paper never helps"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega joyni o‘zgartirishdi?","answers":["the room was noisy"],"explanation":"Noisy so moved — sabab/natija.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["the room was noisy","the library had new chairs","the app stopped working"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["Using a phone for English practice can be convenient because audio and dictionaries are easy to reach.","However, the same device can distract us with messages.","Lola prefers listening to short recordings, while Ali likes reading on paper.","Neither method is best for every task.","Although a learning app helps me practise vocabulary, I still need to use new phrases in conversation.","Last week our study room was noisy, so we moved to the library.","We switched off unrelated notifications and agreed on a clear aim for twenty minutes.","The session went better because we knew what to finish.","This does not mean phones are always bad or paper is always better.","A useful choice depends on the task, the learner and the way the tool is used.","We now discuss the purpose before choosing the device."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"The app is useful. However, messages can distract me. Lola prefers audio, while Ali likes paper. Our room was noisy, so we moved to the library. We worked better because we had a clear aim.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-16.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-16-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Lola nimani afzal ko‘radi?","answers":["audio"],"explanation":"Lola prefers audio.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["audio","paper","video games"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Nega yaxshiroq ishladi?","answers":["a clear aim"],"explanation":"Because clear aim.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["a clear aim","more notifications","a larger phone"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["audio","paper"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","rows":["Lola usuli","Ali usuli"]},{"id":"en-b1-16-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["I took notes because the talk was long."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-16-dictation.mp3","transcript":"I took notes because the talk was long."}]},"writing":{"task":"O‘qish usullaridan ikkitasini foyda va kamchiliklari bilan taqqoslang.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I use both a phone and a notebook to study English. The phone is convenient because I can listen to recordings anywhere. However, messages sometimes distract me. My notebook is useful for keeping a few phrases together, while the phone helps me hear pronunciation. Although an app can show whether a short answer is correct, it cannot tell me everything about my speaking. I therefore practise with a classmate as well. Last week we chose one aim before our session and turned off unrelated notifications. We worked more carefully, so the session was more useful. The tool matters, but the purpose matters too.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["Although the task was difficult, I continued.","The app is useful. However, it can distract me.","Lola likes audio, while Ali prefers reading."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bir fikrga sabab, bir qarama-qarshi nuqtaga esa although/however qo‘shing.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"O‘qish usullaridan ikkitasini foyda va kamchiliklari bilan taqqoslang.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-16-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I continued ___ it was difficult.","answers":["although"],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I took notes ___ the talk was long.","answers":["because"],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The room was noisy, ___ we moved.","answers":["so"],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"However bilan to‘g‘ri yozuv?","answers":["It is useful. However, it distracts me."],"explanation":"Mustaqil fikrlar to‘g‘ri ajratiladi.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["It is useful. However, it distracts me.","It useful however distracts.","Although however but useful."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"While faqat vaqt ma’nosidami?","answers":["No"],"explanation":"Taqqoslash ham bo‘ladi.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["No","Yes","Always"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-16-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The app is useful. However, it can distract me."],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","tokens":["The","app","is","useful.","However,","it","can","distract","me."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I took notes ___ the talk was long.","answers":["because"],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …"},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["I took notes because the talk was long."],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","tokens":["I","took","notes","because","the","talk","was","long."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"However bilan to‘g‘ri yozuv?","answers":["It is useful. However, it distracts me."],"explanation":"Mustaqil fikrlar to‘g‘ri ajratiladi.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","options":["It is useful. However, it distracts me.","It useful however distracts.","Although however but useful."]},{"id":"en-b1-16-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["I practised until the instructions were clear."],"explanation":"Although + gap qarama-qarshi ikki holatni bog‘laydi: Although it was difficult, I continued. Shu gapda qo‘shimcha but ko‘pincha kerak emas. However ikki mustaqil fikrni bog‘lovchi diskurs vositasi. Yozuvda nuqta yoki mos ajratish ishlating; oddiy vergul bilan ikki gapni noto‘g‘ri yopishtirmang. While taqqoslash yoki bir vaqtdagi ikki jarayonni bildirishi mumkin. Because sabab, so natija; sabab va natijani teskari qilib yubormang.","hint":"Although …, … . / … . However, … . / … because … / …, so …","tokens":["I","practised","until","the","instructions","were","clear."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-16","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Subject va object questions: Qabul qiluvchini so‘raydigan savol?","answers":["Who did you send it to?"],"explanation":"Who obyekt, you ega.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Who did you send it to?","Who sent it?","What happened?"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Subject va object questions"},{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Question tags va tasdiqlash ohangi: Inkor gap tagini tanlang: He didn’t call, …","answers":["did he?"],"explanation":"Inkor gap → tasdiq did he.","hint":"You’re ready, aren’t you? / She likes it, doesn’t she?","options":["did he?","didn’t he?","does he?"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Question tags va tasdiqlash ohangi"},{"id":"en-b1-16-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · -ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such: Ot birikmasi bilan to‘g‘ri shakl?","answers":["such an interesting film"],"explanation":"Such + an + sifat + ot.","hint":"I’m interested because it’s interesting. / so good / such a good film","options":["such an interesting film","so an interesting film","such interesting an film"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"-ed va -ing sifatlar; so va such"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-17','en-b1-17',null,3,17,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-17","baseId":"en-b1-17","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":17,"title":"Collocations va phrasal verbsni qo‘llash","objective":"Make progress, take notes, catch up bilan vaziyatni tabiiy ifodalaysiz.","context":"Dars qoldirgan o‘quvchi guruhiga yetib oladi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-16"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang.","Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing.","Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip."],"pattern":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","examples":["I am making progress.","She takes notes during the talk.","We do homework after dinner.","Please hand it in on Friday.","I need to catch up with my class.","Look the word up in a dictionary."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-17-v0","term":"make progress","meaning":"rivojlanmoq","ipa":"/meɪk ˈprəʊɡres/","collocation":"make steady progress","example":"The teacher corrected it to “make progress” and asked him to use the phrase in a new sentence about his own work."},{"id":"en-b1-17-v1","term":"take notes","meaning":"qayd yozmoq","ipa":"/teɪk nəʊts/","collocation":"take clear notes","example":"take clear notes"},{"id":"en-b1-17-v2","term":"hand in","meaning":"topshirmoq","ipa":"/hænd ɪn/","collocation":"hand it in","example":"hand it in"},{"id":"en-b1-17-v3","term":"catch up with","meaning":"yetib olmoq","ipa":"/kætʃ ʌp wɪð/","collocation":"catch up with the class","example":"I need to catch up with my class."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"sentence","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","I am making progress.","She takes notes during the talk."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Dars qoldirgan o‘quvchi guruhiga yetib oladi.","We do homework after dinner.","I need to catch up with my class."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"Please hand it in on Friday.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-17-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-17-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Tabiiy birikmani tanlang.","answers":["take notes"],"explanation":"Take notes.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["take notes","do notes (during a talk)","take homework"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I am ___ progress. (make)","answers":["making"],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["I am making progress."],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","tokens":["I","am","making","progress."]},{"id":"en-b1-17-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Please hand in it.","answers":["Please hand it in."],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["rivojlanmoq","qayd yozmoq","topshirmoq","yetib olmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","left":["make progress","take notes","hand in","catch up with"],"options":["rivojlanmoq","qayd yozmoq","topshirmoq","yetib olmoq"]}],"reading":{"title":"Collocations va phrasal verbsni qo‘llash — vaziyat","text":"Ali missed two lessons while visiting his grandparents. When he returned, he wanted to catch up with his class without copying all the answers. Lola gave him her notes and explained the main task. He looked up unfamiliar words and tried one example on his own. During the next talk, he took notes using short phrases rather than writing every sentence. His teacher asked him to hand the work in on Friday. Ali was making progress, but he still confused some common word combinations. He wrote “do progress” in one paragraph. The teacher corrected it to “make progress” and asked him to use the phrase in a new sentence about his own work. Learning the combination inside a real message helped him remember it. By Friday, he had finished the missing task and could explain the idea to another student.","sentences":["Ali missed two lessons while visiting his grandparents.","When he returned, he wanted to catch up with his class without copying all the answers.","Lola gave him her notes and explained the main task.","He looked up unfamiliar words and tried one example on his own.","During the next talk, he took notes using short phrases rather than writing every sentence.","His teacher asked him to hand the work in on Friday.","Ali was making progress, but he still confused some common word combinations.","He wrote “do progress” in one paragraph.","The teacher corrected it to “make progress” and asked him to use the phrase in a new sentence about his own work.","Learning the combination inside a real message helped him remember it.","By Friday, he had finished the missing task and could explain the idea to another student."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-17-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Ali nega javoblarni ko‘chirmadi?","answers":["he wanted to understand and catch up"],"explanation":"O‘z misolini sinaydi, maqsad tushunish.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["he wanted to understand and catch up","the teacher hid all notes","he disliked the subject"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Qanday so‘z birikmasi tuzatildi?","answers":["do progress → make progress"],"explanation":"Make progress tabiiy birikma.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["do progress → make progress","take notes → make notes only","hand in → get up"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["Ali missed two lessons while visiting his grandparents.","When he returned, he wanted to catch up with his class without copying all the answers.","Lola gave him her notes and explained the main task.","He looked up unfamiliar words and tried one example on his own.","During the next talk, he took notes using short phrases rather than writing every sentence.","His teacher asked him to hand the work in on Friday.","Ali was making progress, but he still confused some common word combinations.","He wrote “do progress” in one paragraph.","The teacher corrected it to “make progress” and asked him to use the phrase in a new sentence about his own work.","Learning the combination inside a real message helped him remember it.","By Friday, he had finished the missing task and could explain the idea to another student."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"Ali needs to catch up with the class. He takes notes, looks up unfamiliar words, and does homework. He is making progress. The teacher asks him to hand it in on Friday.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-17.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-17-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Topshirish kuni?","answers":["Friday"],"explanation":"Hand it in on Friday.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["Friday","Monday","Sunday"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qaysi birikma rivojlanishni bildiradi?","answers":["make progress"],"explanation":"Make progress.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["make progress","do progress","take progress"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["Friday","catch up"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","rows":["Muddat","Ortda qolish yechimi"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["Please hand it in on Friday."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-17-dictation.mp3","transcript":"Please hand it in on Friday."}]},"writing":{"task":"Dars qoldirgandan keyingi rejangizni kamida to‘rtta tabiiy birikma bilan yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I missed two lessons last week, so I need to catch up with my class. First, I will read the teacher’s summary and take notes on the main points. I will look unfamiliar words up and try one exercise without looking at the answer. Then I will do the homework and ask a classmate to check whether my explanation is clear. I have to hand it in on Friday. I am already making progress because I can describe the first topic in my own words. I will keep the useful phrases in my notebook and use them in a new message tomorrow.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["I am making progress.","She takes notes during the talk.","We do homework after dinner."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"O‘qish muammosini ayting va to‘rtta birikma bilan yechim taklif qiling.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Dars qoldirgandan keyingi rejangizni kamida to‘rtta tabiiy birikma bilan yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-17-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ homework","answers":["do"],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ progress","answers":["make"],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Hand ___ in. (it)","answers":["it"],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ortda qolgan guruhga yetishmoq?","answers":["catch up with"],"explanation":"Catch up with class.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["catch up with","look down at","take after only"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Lug‘atda so‘z tekshirish?","answers":["look it up"],"explanation":"Look it up, olmosh o‘rtada.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["look it up","look up it","hand it off"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-17-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["She takes notes during the talk."],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","tokens":["She","takes","notes","during","the","talk."]},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ progress","answers":["make"],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with"},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Please hand it in on Friday."],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","tokens":["Please","hand","it","in","on","Friday."]},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ortda qolgan guruhga yetishmoq?","answers":["catch up with"],"explanation":"Catch up with class.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","options":["catch up with","look down at","take after only"]},{"id":"en-b1-17-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Look the word up in a dictionary."],"explanation":"Collocation birga tabiiy ishlatiladigan so‘zlar: make progress, take notes, do homework. Har birini o‘zbekchadan so‘zma-so‘z ko‘chirmang. Catch up with — ortda qolgan qismga yetishish; hand in — topshirish; look up — tekshirib topish. Birikmani kontekst va to‘ldiruvchi bilan o‘rganing. Ajraladigan phrasal verbda olmosh o‘rtada: hand it in, look it up. Catch up with classmates esa boshqa qolip.","hint":"make progress / take notes / do homework / hand it in / catch up with","tokens":["Look","the","word","up","in","a","dictionary."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-17","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-18','en-b1-18',null,3,18,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-18","baseId":"en-b1-18","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":18,"title":"Tajriba, fikr va asoslangan tavsiya","objective":"O‘z tajribangizga tayangan fikrni sabab, misol va cheklov bilan ifodalaysiz.","context":"Maktab klubiga yangi o‘qish usuli tavsiya qilinadi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-17"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas.","O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi.","B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim."],"pattern":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","examples":["I think short daily practice is useful.","It helps because the task is manageable.","For example, I remember more phrases now.","However, different learners need different plans.","I suggest trying it for a week.","What would you change in this plan?"],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-18-v0","term":"manageable","meaning":"bajarish mumkin bo‘lgan","ipa":"/ˈmænɪdʒəbəl/","collocation":"a manageable task","example":"It helps because the task is manageable."},{"id":"en-b1-18-v1","term":"suggest","meaning":"taklif qilmoq","ipa":"/səˈdʒest/","collocation":"suggest trying","example":"I suggest trying it for a week."},{"id":"en-b1-18-v2","term":"experience","meaning":"tajriba","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪəriəns/","collocation":"personal experience","example":"personal experience"},{"id":"en-b1-18-v3","term":"balanced","meaning":"muvozanatli","ipa":"/ˈbælənst/","collocation":"a balanced view","example":"a balanced view"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","I think short daily practice is useful.","It helps because the task is manageable."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Maktab klubiga yangi o‘qish usuli tavsiya qilinadi.","For example, I remember more phrases now.","I suggest trying it for a week."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"However, different learners need different plans.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-18-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-18-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Eng muvozanatli xulosa?","answers":["Try the routine and compare results for your needs."],"explanation":"Dalil va cheklovga tayangan xulosa.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["Try the routine and compare results for your needs.","Everyone must follow my plan.","Only minutes prove your level."]},{"id":"en-b1-18-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I suggest ___ it for a week. (try)","answers":["trying"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["I think short daily practice is useful."],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","tokens":["I","think","short","daily","practice","is","useful."]},{"id":"en-b1-18-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"My method works for me, so it must work for everyone.","answers":["My method works for me, but it may not work for everyone."],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["bajarish mumkin bo‘lgan","taklif qilmoq","tajriba","muvozanatli"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","left":["manageable","suggest","experience","balanced"],"options":["bajarish mumkin bo‘lgan","taklif qilmoq","tajriba","muvozanatli"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["manageable","suggest","experience","balanced"],"options":["a manageable task","suggest trying","personal experience","a balanced view"],"answers":["a manageable task","suggest trying","personal experience","a balanced view"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."}],"reading":{"title":"Tajriba, fikr va asoslangan tavsiya — vaziyat","text":"Our reading club is deciding whether to practise for a long time once a week or for a short time every day. I used to study only at weekends and often forgot the words I had learned. This term I have been practising for fifteen minutes each evening. I have remembered more useful phrases, and I can use some of them in conversation. For me, the smaller task is easier to start. However, a friend has a busy evening routine and prefers two longer sessions. Her plan works because she reviews the material between meetings. We should not choose one method only because it worked for one person. I suggest trying a short daily routine for a week, recording the tasks we complete, and then comparing what we can actually do. The aim is not to count minutes alone but to notice whether we understand and use the language better.","sentences":["Our reading club is deciding whether to practise for a long time once a week or for a short time every day.","I used to study only at weekends and often forgot the words I had learned.","This term I have been practising for fifteen minutes each evening.","I have remembered more useful phrases, and I can use some of them in conversation.","For me, the smaller task is easier to start.","However, a friend has a busy evening routine and prefers two longer sessions.","Her plan works because she reviews the material between meetings.","We should not choose one method only because it worked for one person.","I suggest trying a short daily routine for a week, recording the tasks we complete, and then comparing what we can actually do.","The aim is not to count minutes alone but to notice whether we understand and use the language better."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-18-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Muallif nima taklif qiladi?","answers":["test a routine and compare actual skills"],"explanation":"Sinov va real ko‘nikma asosidagi taqqoslash.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["test a routine and compare actual skills","force one method on everyone","count only minutes"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega ehtiyotkor xulosa beradi?","answers":["learners have different routines"],"explanation":"Do‘stining boshqa rejasi ishlaydi.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["learners have different routines","no method can ever work","the club has no members"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["Our reading club is deciding whether to practise for a long time once a week or for a short time every day.","I used to study only at weekends and often forgot the words I had learned.","This term I have been practising for fifteen minutes each evening.","I have remembered more useful phrases, and I can use some of them in conversation.","For me, the smaller task is easier to start.","However, a friend has a busy evening routine and prefers two longer sessions.","Her plan works because she reviews the material between meetings.","We should not choose one method only because it worked for one person.","I suggest trying a short daily routine for a week, recording the tasks we complete, and then comparing what we can actually do.","The aim is not to count minutes alone but to notice whether we understand and use the language better."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"I have tried fifteen minutes of practice each day, and I remember more phrases. However, my friend prefers two longer sessions. I suggest testing a routine for a week and comparing what we can do, not just how many minutes we study.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-18.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-18-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qancha kundalik vaqt?","answers":["fifteen minutes"],"explanation":"Fifteen, fifty emas.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["fifteen minutes","fifty minutes","two hours"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Nimani solishtirish kerak?","answers":["what learners can do"],"explanation":"Actual ability.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["what learners can do","only minutes","only word count"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["a week","fifteen minutes"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","rows":["Sinov muddati","Kunlik vaqt"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["However, different learners need different plans."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-18-dictation.mp3","transcript":"However, different learners need different plans."}]},"writing":{"task":"B1 loyiha: o‘qish usuli haqida tajriba, dalil, boshqa fikr va amaliy tavsiya yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I think short daily practice is useful because it is easier to fit into a normal day. I used to study only at the weekend and forgot many phrases. This term I have been practising for fifteen minutes each evening, and I can use more phrases in conversation. For example, I now ask for directions without reading a model. However, my friend prefers two longer sessions because her evenings are busy. I suggest testing a routine for one week and recording what we can actually do. A method should help us understand and communicate, not simply collect a large number of minutes.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["I think short daily practice is useful.","It helps because the task is manageable.","For example, I remember more phrases now."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Tavsiyangizni ikki daqiqagacha ayting, e’tirozga javob bering va yakuniy fikrni aniqlashtiring.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Sherigingizning bir boshqa fikrini tinglang, uni xolis qayta ayting va tavsiyangizga qo‘shing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-18-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I have been ___ daily. (practise)","answers":["practising"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I suggest ___ it. (try)","answers":["trying"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"It helps ___ the task is manageable.","answers":["because"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Dalil qaysi?","answers":["a specific example from experience"],"explanation":"Misol fikrni asoslaydi.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["a specific example from experience","only “I think”","a repeated opinion"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Bitta shaxs tajribasi hamma uchun kafolatmi?","answers":["No"],"explanation":"Cheklovni aytish zarur.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["No","Yes","Always"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-18-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["It helps because the task is manageable."],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","tokens":["It","helps","because","the","task","is","manageable."]},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I suggest ___ it. (try)","answers":["trying"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … ."},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["However, different learners need different plans."],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","tokens":["However,","different","learners","need","different","plans."]},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Dalil qaysi?","answers":["a specific example from experience"],"explanation":"Misol fikrni asoslaydi.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","options":["a specific example from experience","only “I think”","a repeated opinion"]},{"id":"en-b1-18-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["What would you change in this plan?"],"explanation":"Opinion → reason → example → balanced conclusion fikrni tushunarli rivojlantiradi. I think deyishning o‘zi dalil emas. O‘z tajribangizni boshqa odamlar uchun universal natija deb bermang. For me, in our group, may help kabi chegaralar aniqlikni oshiradi. B1da bog‘langan nutq maqsad: o‘tmish tajribasi, hozirgi natija, tavsiya va savol. Mukammal gap yodlashdan ko‘ra ma’no va aloqa muhim.","hint":"I think … because … . For example, … . However, … . I suggest … .","tokens":["What","would","you","change","in","this","plan?"]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-18","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":true,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-01','en-b2-01',null,4,1,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-01","baseId":"en-b2-01","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":1,"title":"Aspect: natija va jarayonni tanlash","objective":"Ish natijasi va vaqt davomida kechgan jarayonni aniq farqlaysiz.","context":"Mahalla kutubxonasini yangilash loyihasi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-18"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi.","I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi.","For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang."],"pattern":"have completed / have been working","examples":["We have repaired three shelves.","We have been repairing shelves all morning.","She has known the manager for years.","I have been checking the labels.","The team has collected enough books.","How many labels have you checked?"],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-01-v0","term":"outcome","meaning":"yakuniy natija","ipa":"/ˈaʊtkʌm/","collocation":"a measurable outcome","example":"a measurable outcome"},{"id":"en-b2-01-v1","term":"ongoing","meaning":"davom etayotgan","ipa":"/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ/","collocation":"ongoing work","example":"ongoing work"},{"id":"en-b2-01-v2","term":"estimate","meaning":"taxminiy baho","ipa":"/ˈestɪmət/","collocation":"a time estimate","example":"The team’s next estimate will include inspection time instead of treating it as a delay with no value."},{"id":"en-b2-01-v3","term":"evidence","meaning":"dalil","ipa":"/ˈevɪdəns/","collocation":"clear evidence","example":"clear evidence"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"timeline","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["have completed / have been working","We have repaired three shelves.","We have been repairing shelves all morning."],"timeline":[{"why":"Have repaired three shelves tugagan ish miqdorini hozirgi natija sifatida ko‘rsatadi.","events":[{"kind":"point","x":210,"label":"Uch tokcha tayyor"},{"kind":"link","from":210,"to":320,"label":"Hozirgi natija"}]},{"why":"Have been repairing all morning bajarilish jarayoni va davomiyligini ajratadi. Tugagan tokchalar soni bu gapda yo‘q.","events":[{"kind":"span","from":90,"to":320,"label":"Ertalab davom etgan ish"}]}]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The report needs two measures.","Three shelves are repaired, and inspection continues.","Results and effort answer different questions."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"I have been checking the labels.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-01-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-01-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: We have ___ three shelves. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["repaired","repairing","repair"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We have ___ three shelves. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working"},{"id":"en-b2-01-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["We have repaired three shelves."],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working","tokens":["We","have","repaired","three","shelves."]},{"id":"en-b2-01-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We have been knowing the manager for years.","answers":["We have known the manager for years."],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working"},{"id":"en-b2-01-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["yakuniy natija","davom etayotgan","taxminiy baho","dalil"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"have completed / have been working","left":["outcome","ongoing","estimate","evidence"],"options":["yakuniy natija","davom etayotgan","taxminiy baho","dalil"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Jarayonga urg‘u bering: We started checking books four hours ago and are still checking them.","answers":["We have been checking books for four hours."],"hint":"have completed / have been working","explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi."},{"id":"en-b2-01-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The report needs two measures.","Three shelves are repaired, and inspection continues.","Results and effort answer different questions."],"answers":["The report needs two measures.\nThree shelves are repaired, and inspection continues.\nResults and effort answer different questions."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"The library team has repaired three shelves, but the work has taken longer than expected. Volunteers have been checking damaged books all morning. A photograph of the busy room shows effort, yet it does not tell us how many books can safely return to the shelves. The manager therefore records both time spent and usable results. One volunteer argues that only completed work matters. Another points out that checking an unsafe shelf can prevent an accident even if no new shelf is finished. Both views are reasonable, but neither is sufficient alone. A progress report should explain what has been completed, what is still being investigated, and why the remaining work is necessary. The team’s next estimate will include inspection time instead of treating it as a delay with no value.","sentences":["The library team has repaired three shelves, but the work has taken longer than expected.","Volunteers have been checking damaged books all morning.","A photograph of the busy room shows effort, yet it does not tell us how many books can safely return to the shelves.","The manager therefore records both time spent and usable results.","One volunteer argues that only completed work matters.","Another points out that checking an unsafe shelf can prevent an accident even if no new shelf is finished.","Both views are reasonable, but neither is sufficient alone.","A progress report should explain what has been completed, what is still being investigated, and why the remaining work is necessary.","The team’s next estimate will include inspection time instead of treating it as a delay with no value."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-01-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Muallif nimani tavsiya qiladi?","answers":["record both effort and usable results"],"explanation":"Har ikki o‘lchov maqsad uchun zarur.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["record both effort and usable results","count only finished shelves","use photographs instead of records"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Inspection qanday baholanadi?","answers":["valuable even without a finished shelf"],"explanation":"Tekshiruv xavfni aniqlaydi.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["valuable even without a finished shelf","always a waste","proof that all shelves are safe"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["The library team has repaired three shelves, but the work has taken longer than expected.","Volunteers have been checking damaged books all morning.","A photograph of the busy room shows effort, yet it does not tell us how many books can safely return to the shelves.","The manager therefore records both time spent and usable results.","One volunteer argues that only completed work matters.","Another points out that checking an unsafe shelf can prevent an accident even if no new shelf is finished.","Both views are reasonable, but neither is sufficient alone.","A progress report should explain what has been completed, what is still being investigated, and why the remaining work is necessary.","The team’s next estimate will include inspection time instead of treating it as a delay with no value."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Manager: We have repaired three shelves. Volunteer: We have been checking books for four hours. Manager: That work matters, but we need to record which books are safe. Volunteer: Then the report should show both the completed repairs and the inspection still in progress.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-01.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-01-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qancha vaqt tekshirildi?","answers":["four hours"],"explanation":"Four hours.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["four hours","three hours","four days"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Hisobotda nima bo‘lsin?","answers":["results and ongoing inspection"],"explanation":"Ikki jihat ham aytiladi.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["results and ongoing inspection","only a photo","only delays"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["three","four hours"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"have completed / have been working","rows":["Tokchalar","Tekshiruv vaqti"]},{"id":"en-b2-01-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["I have been checking the labels."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"have completed / have been working","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-01-dictation.mp3","transcript":"I have been checking the labels."}]},"writing":{"task":"Progress report yozing: tugallangan ish, davom etgan jarayon, dalil va keyingi vaqt taxmini.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":90,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Our team has repaired three shelves and returned twenty books to use. We have been checking the remaining books since Monday, and some need further inspection. The work has taken longer than we expected because checking safety is part of the task, rather than an unnecessary delay. A photograph shows that volunteers are busy, but it cannot replace a record of usable results. We recommend recording both completed repairs and inspection time. This will help the next team estimate the remaining work more accurately. We should also explain why an unfinished inspection may still be valuable: it can prevent an unsafe bookcase from returning to use.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["We have repaired three shelves.","We have been repairing shelves all morning.","She has known the manager for years."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Ishga ketgan vaqt natijaga teng emas degan fikrni dalil bilan muhokama qiling.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Progress report yozing: tugallangan ish, davom etgan jarayon, dalil va keyingi vaqt taxmini.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-01-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We have ___ three shelves. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working"},{"id":"en-b2-01-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We have been ___ all morning. (work)","answers":["working"],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working"},{"id":"en-b2-01-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She has ___ him for years. (know)","answers":["known"],"explanation":"Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi. I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi. For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.","hint":"have completed / have been working"},{"id":"en-b2-01-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Miqdorga e’tibor qaysi?","answers":["We have checked twenty books."],"explanation":"Twenty tugallangan miqdor.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["We have checked twenty books.","We have been checking books.","We are checking books."]},{"id":"en-b2-01-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Inspection qanday baholanadi?","answers":["valuable even without a finished shelf"],"explanation":"Tekshiruv xavfni aniqlaydi.","hint":"have completed / have been working","options":["valuable even without a finished shelf","always a waste","proof that all shelves are safe"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-01-exit-b0","type":"order